Control is an illusion, the universe is a dance between nothing and something, it is the movement created when the two relate in such in a way it births something entirely third. We must cultivate the internal gnomon to guide us, that prevents us from devolving into pure consumption. In every act we must take the second between stimulus and response to define our actions and to proceed with virtue. This cannot not be something forced, humans are not Gods of order, we are not equations to be corrected, or cogs to be fitted in place, we are animals given reason, we are the universe itself given relation and individuality to explore our environment. We often ask why God does not act, but they do through you, through me, we must come to understand the only true difference between us is the one we build ourselves. That we are all part of the same being seeking relation across multitudes, that to try to control and consume without reason, virtue, or creation is antithetical to not only our own nature, but the nature of reality as a whole. The universe is defined by relation, by creation vs consumption, and our own struggle as a species between Earth and Empire. We must stop seeking control, control of life, of fate, of others, of Earth, and start the seekin internal cultivation of self, we must stop asking does this give me more power, more control and instead ask what this creates and what does it consume. We MUST STOP being consumers who long for control and instead be the creators of our own emancipation.

-Stowyn Leir(Stowynn Lār.)
